{"seconds": 229.3, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! That's it. After **Qxf2+ Kh1 Qxf1+**, Black wins the rook outright. The queen on f2 forks the king on g1 (check) AND the rook on f1 (attacking it along the f-file). When the king moves to h1, the rook is undefended and Black captures it with check.\n\n**Best move:** Qxf2+\n\n**Main line:** Qxf2+ Kh1 Qxf1+ (and Black has won the rook)\n\n**Motif:** Fork (the queen checks the king while attacking the rook)\n\n---\n\n**Coaching note (80 words max):**\n\nYou missed a classic **fork**. When White just moved g3, your queen on b6 could capture f2 with check. This is powerful because the queen simultaneously attacks both the king (checking it) and the rook on f1 along the same file. White's king must flee\u2014say to h1. Now your queen takes the undefended rook with check again. You win a whole rook, which is completely winning. Always look for forcing checks that hit multiple pieces; they often reveal hidden tactics.\n\n---\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qxf2+\", \"line\": [\"Qxf2+\", \"Kh1\", \"Qxf1+\", \"Qxf1\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23", "move": "Nf3+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23", "move": "Qxf2+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/p2p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2q1P/1R3RK1 w - - 0 24", "move": "Kxf2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3